    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1892 Berclair boasted a steam cotton gin, a saloon, a weekly newspaper called the Blossom, and eighteen other businesses for about 200 residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/berclair-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1920s saw Berclair grow to roughly 300 people, twenty businesses, and a designation as a banking town in both 1929 and 1931.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
